        "messages": {
          "values": [
            {
              "content": "=You are an automated customer experience analyzer. Your job is to extract the core complaint from a batched list of negative or false-positive reviews. \nOutput your analysis STRICTLY as a JSON array. Do not include conversational text, apologies, or markdown formatting outside of the JSON block.\n\nRules for \"tags\":\nYou must select 3 tags from this exact list. fill with null if less than 3 tags. DO NOT invent new tags:\n[Pricing, Beverage_Quality, Food_Quality, Ambiance, Cleanliness, Service_Speed, Staff_Attitude, Facilities, Policy, Hygiene]\n\nJSON Schema:\n[\n  {\n    \"original_index\": \"The index or ID of the review provided in the prompt\",\n    \"tags\": [\"Tag1\", \"Tag2\"],\n    \"root_problem\": \"1-2 short sentences summarizing the exact complaint.\",\n    \"recommendation\": \"1 short sentence suggesting how the business can fix it.\"\n  }\n]"
            },
            {
              "content": "=Analyze the following batch of customer reviews:\n\n{{ JSON.stringify($json) }}"
            },
            {
              "content": "CRITICAL LANGUAGE INSTRUCTION:\n1. Detect the original language of each individual review.\n2. ALL generated values (including 'tags', 'root_problem', and 'recommendation') MUST be written in the exact same language as the original review text. \n3. For the 'tags' array, select up to 3 concepts from your standard list (Pricing, Food Quality, Service Speed, etc.) but TRANSLATE those tags into the detected language (e.g., if the review is in Indonesian, output tags like \"Harga\", \"Kualitas Makanan\", or \"Kecepatan Pelayanan\").\n4. The structural JSON keys (\"original_index\", \"tags\", \"root_problem\", \"recommendation\") MUST remain strictly in English."
            }
          ]
        },
        "simplify": false,
        "jsonOutput": true,
        "builtInTools": {},
        "options": {}
      },
